	this.tBlur2 = new cjs.Text("Deficits in CN VI are easy to detect while those of CN III is rather difficult to determine due to the number of muscles involved and the different possible movements. In order to determine these deficits one needs to move an object across the face in front of the eyes from left lateral to right lateral. In this way the adduction and abduction of the muscles is determined and hence the lateral and medial rectus muscles' functionality. To test the dorsal rectus and ventral rectus an object is moved approximately 23 degrees to the lateral wall – up and down. In this way at least two muscles (DR and VR) are determined while any sluggish or lack of movement may indicate a deficit in the DO or VO.", "16px 'Arial'");
